// Chapter 6 - Parsing Expressions
//
// The interpreter does not evaluate anything yet, so running this file prints
// the *syntax tree* the parser built, in the fully-parenthesised form that
// chapter 5's AST printer produces. Reading it is how you check that
// precedence and associativity came out right.
//
//   ./scripts/lox.sh examples/ch06_parsing.lox
//
// Only one expression per file can be parsed in chapter 6 (statements arrive
// in chapter 8), so this file holds one expression that exercises every
// precedence level at once:
//
//   unary binds tighter than factor  ->  -4 sits under the *
//   factor binds tighter than term   ->  3 * -4 sits under the +
//   term binds tighter than comparison
//   comparison binds tighter than equality
//
// Expected output:
//
//   (== (< 1.0 (+ 2.0 (* 3.0 (- 4.0)))) false)

1 < 2 + 3 * -4 == false
